---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Hold the shield while real users keep shopping" hint="A shop gets 4,000 requests per second from real people. At second 10 an attack starts and runs for 40 seconds. Pick the attack and the defences, and watch the origin, the real users who get blocked by mistake, and how long mitigation takes.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default is an <b>HTTP flood from 20,000 bots</b> with 8 points of presence, a per-IP limit of 100 and a balanced WAF. The origin is at about <b>580% of its capacity</b>, half of the real users fail, and it is <b>never mitigated</b>. Two things are wrong: the 8 sites can handle only about 96,000 requests per second, less than the flood, and each bot sends so few requests that it looks like a person to a per-IP limit.</li>
    <li>Switch the challenge to <b>when an attack is detected</b> and raise the points of presence to 16: the bots are mostly stopped after <b>12 seconds</b>, the time it takes to notice and push the rule. Set the challenge to <b>always on</b> and mitigation is instant, but 3% of real visitors fail the challenge, even with no attack.</li>
    <li>Pick <b>cache-busting</b>: with a cache keyed by the full URL nothing ever hits, and the origin is safe at once only with <b>normalized cache keys</b>. Pick <b>volumetric</b>: only about <b>20 or more points of presence</b> absorb 300 Gbps. Untick the <b>lockdown</b> and the attacker finds the origin address and bypasses every defence.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg ddb" data-ddb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Attack <select class="pg-in" data-attack>
        <option value="http" selected>HTTP flood from 20,000 bot IPs</option>
        <option value="bust">Cache-busting flood (random query strings)</option>
        <option value="vol">Volumetric UDP flood (300 Gbps)</option>
        <option value="slow">Low-and-slow connections (150,000)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Points of presence (anycast) <input type="range" min="1" max="40" value="8" data-pops /> <b data-popsval></b></label>
      <label>Per-IP limit <select class="pg-in" data-rate>
        <option value="0">off</option><option value="5">5 requests/s</option><option value="10">10 requests/s</option><option value="20">20 requests/s</option><option value="50">50 requests/s</option><option value="100" selected>100 requests/s</option><option value="300">300 requests/s</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Cache <select class="pg-in" data-cache>
        <option value="off">off</option><option value="full" selected>keyed by the full URL</option><option value="norm">keyed by the normalized URL</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Challenge page <select class="pg-in" data-chal>
        <option value="off" selected>never</option><option value="auto">when an attack is detected</option><option value="always">always on</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>WAF and bot scoring <select class="pg-in" data-waf>
        <option value="lenient">lenient</option><option value="balanced" selected>balanced</option><option value="strict">strict</option>
      </select></label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" checked data-lock /> Origin accepts only the edge (lockdown)</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Peak origin load</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Real requests blocked</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Attack traffic that got through</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Time to mitigate</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box">
        <h3>Origin load, as a share of its capacity</h3>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 240 70" role="img" aria-label="Origin load over 60 seconds as a share of capacity, with the attack shaded between seconds 10 and 50 and a dashed line at 100% capacity" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-height:150px">
          <rect x="40" y="0" width="160" height="62" style="fill:var(--bad);opacity:.12"></rect>
          <line x1="0" y1="62" x2="240" y2="62" style="stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:.5"></line>
          <line x1="0" y1="41.3" x2="240" y2="41.3" style="stroke:var(--bad);stroke-width:.6;stroke-dasharray:3 3"></line>
          <polyline data-line1 fill="none" style="stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.5" points=""></polyline>
          <text x="2" y="38.5" font-size="6" style="fill:var(--muted)">100% = capacity</text>
          <text x="2" y="8" font-size="6" style="fill:var(--muted)">300% or more</text>
          <text x="2" y="69" font-size="6" style="fill:var(--muted)">0 s</text>
          <text x="238" y="69" font-size="6" text-anchor="end" style="fill:var(--muted)">60 s</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="pg-box">
        <h3>Real requests that fail</h3>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 240 70" role="img" aria-label="Share of real requests that fail over 60 seconds, with the attack shaded between seconds 10 and 50" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-height:150px">
          <rect x="40" y="0" width="160" height="62" style="fill:var(--bad);opacity:.12"></rect>
          <line x1="0" y1="62" x2="240" y2="62" style="stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:.5"></line>
          <polyline data-line2 fill="none" style="stroke:var(--bad);stroke-width:1.5" points=""></polyline>
          <text x="2" y="8" font-size="6" style="fill:var(--muted)">100% of real requests</text>
          <text x="2" y="69" font-size="6" style="fill:var(--muted)">0 s</text>
          <text x="238" y="69" font-size="6" text-anchor="end" style="fill:var(--muted)">60 s</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: one step per second for 60 seconds, and the attack runs from second 10 to 50. Real traffic is 4,000 requests per second, 60% of them for cacheable pages (95% hit rate), and 2,000 open connections. The origin handles 6,000 requests per second, 10,000 connections and 10 Gbps. A point of presence handles 25 Gbps, 20,000 requests per second and 15,000 connections, and because an attack is concentrated in a few regions only 60% of that is usable. Attacks: HTTP flood is 120,000 requests per second from 20,000 IPs at 6 each, and 30% of its URLs are cacheable. Cache-busting is 80,000 per second from 16,000 IPs at 5 each, all for cacheable pages with a random query string. Real clients burst when a page loads: 70% of requests come from IPs that peak at 10 requests per second, 20% at 25 and 10% (offices behind one address) at 100, so a limit below a group's peak blocks the excess. The per-IP limit takes 2 seconds to start. The WAF stops 15%, 50% or 85% of bot requests (lenient, balanced, strict), and wrongly blocks 0.2%, 1% or 5% of real ones. The challenge stops 94% of bots and loses 3% of real visitors. When set to detect, it starts after 8 seconds of overload plus 4 seconds to push the rule. Low-and-slow connections are held at the edge, and a stricter WAF closes them sooner, leaving 100%, 40% or 6% of them open. Without the lockdown, 40% of the bots (all of the volumetric flood) find the origin address and bypass the edge.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ddb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    // SIM-START
    type Cfg = { attack: string; pops: number; rate: number; cache: string; chal: string; waf: string; lock: boolean };
    const ATTACKS: Record<string, { gbps: number; rps: number; perIp: number; cacheable: number; busting: boolean; conns: number }> = {
      vol: { gbps: 300, rps: 0, perIp: 0, cacheable: 0, busting: false, conns: 0 },
      http: { gbps: 0, rps: 120000, perIp: 6, cacheable: 0.3, busting: false, conns: 0 },
      bust: { gbps: 0, rps: 80000, perIp: 5, cacheable: 1, busting: true, conns: 0 },
      slow: { gbps: 0, rps: 0, perIp: 0, cacheable: 0, busting: false, conns: 150000 },
    };
    const WAF: Record<string, { catch: number; fp: number; hold: number }> = { lenient: { catch: 0.15, fp: 0.002, hold: 1 }, balanced: { catch: 0.5, fp: 0.01, hold: 0.4 }, strict: { catch: 0.85, fp: 0.05, hold: 0.06 } };
    const K = { realRps: 4000, realCacheable: 0.6, hit: 0.95, realConns: 2000, originRps: 6000, originConns: 10000, originGbps: 10, popGbps: 25, popRps: 20000, popConns: 15000, effect: 0.6, start: 10, end: 50, secs: 60, rlDelay: 2, detect: 8, push: 4, botPass: 0.06, chalLoss: 0.03, direct: 0.4 };
    const STRESS_LOAD = 0.8; const EDGE_OK = 0.98; // origin load, and edge pass rate, that count as stress
    const GROUPS = [[0.7, 10], [0.2, 25], [0.1, 100]]; // share of real requests, and the peak requests per second of one IP in that group
    const rlFalse = (t: number) => (t === 0 ? 0 : GROUPS.reduce((s, g) => s + g[0] * Math.max(0, 1 - t / g[1]), 0));
    function run(c: Cfg) {
      const a = ATTACKS[c.attack]; const w = WAF[c.waf];
      const edgeGbps = K.popGbps * c.pops * K.effect; const edgeRps = K.popRps * c.pops * K.effect; const edgeConns = K.popConns * c.pops * K.effect;
      const rows: { t: number; on: boolean; stress: boolean; load: number; blocked: number; reach: number; total: number; okEdge: number; directLoad: number }[] = [];
      let stressedPrev = false; let count = 0; let chalAt = Infinity;
      const total = a.rps + a.conns + a.gbps;
      for (let t = 0; t < K.secs; t++) {
        const on = t >= K.start && t < K.end;
        if (c.chal === 'auto' && on && chalAt === Infinity) { count = stressedPrev ? count + 1 : 0; if (count >= K.detect) chalAt = t + K.push; }
        const httpAttack = c.attack === 'http' || c.attack === 'bust';
        const chalOn = on && httpAttack && (c.chal === 'always' || t >= chalAt);
        const chalCost = c.chal === 'always' || chalOn; // an always-on challenge also costs visitors when nothing is wrong
        const direct = on && !c.lock ? (c.attack === 'vol' ? 1 : K.direct) : 0;
        const via = on ? 1 - direct : 0;
        // The edge shares its bandwidth, request capacity and connection table between real users and the attack.
        const okGbps = Math.min(1, edgeGbps / (a.gbps * via + 1));
        const okRps = Math.min(1, edgeRps / (K.realRps + a.rps * via));
        const okConn = Math.min(1, edgeConns / (K.realConns + a.conns * via * w.hold));
        const okEdge = okGbps * okRps * okConn;
        const rlOn = on && c.rate > 0 && t >= K.start + K.rlDelay;
        const aRl = rlOn && a.perIp ? Math.min(1, c.rate / a.perIp) : 1; // a limit above what each bot sends stops nothing
        const rReal = c.rate > 0 ? 1 - rlFalse(c.rate) : 1;
        const aWaf = httpAttack ? 1 - w.catch : 1; const rWaf = 1 - w.fp;
        const aChal = chalOn ? K.botPass : 1; const rChal = chalCost ? 1 - K.chalLoss : 1;
        const hitReal = c.cache === 'off' ? 0 : K.hit;
        const hitAtk = c.cache === 'off' || (a.busting && c.cache === 'full') ? 0 : K.hit; // a random query string never hits a cache keyed by the full URL
        const realCached = K.realCacheable * hitReal;
        const realOrigin = K.realRps * okEdge * rReal * rWaf * rChal * (1 - realCached);
        const atkOrigin = a.rps * via * okEdge * aRl * aWaf * aChal * (1 - a.cacheable * hitAtk) + a.rps * direct;
        const slowOrigin = a.conns * direct;
        const directLoad = Math.max((a.rps * direct) / K.originRps, slowOrigin / K.originConns, (a.gbps * direct) / K.originGbps);
        const load = Math.max((realOrigin + atkOrigin) / K.originRps, (K.realConns * okEdge + slowOrigin) / K.originConns, (a.gbps * direct + 1) / K.originGbps);
        const okOrigin = Math.min(1, 1 / load);
        const realOk = okEdge * rReal * rWaf * rChal * (realCached + (1 - realCached) * okOrigin);
        stressedPrev = on && (load > STRESS_LOAD || okEdge < EDGE_OK);
        const reach = a.rps ? atkOrigin : a.conns ? slowOrigin : a.gbps * direct;
        rows.push({ t, on, stress: on && (load > 1 || okEdge < EDGE_OK), load: on ? load : (K.realRps * (1 - realCached)) / K.originRps, blocked: 1 - realOk, reach: on ? reach : 0, total, okEdge: on ? okEdge : 1, directLoad: on ? directLoad : 0 });
      }
      const win = rows.filter((r) => r.on);
      const avg = (f: (r: (typeof rows)[number]) => number) => win.reduce((s, r) => s + f(r), 0) / win.length;
      const bad = win.map((r) => r.stress);
      let tm: number | null = null;
      if (!bad.some(Boolean)) tm = 0;
      else if (!bad[bad.length - 1]) { let i = bad.length - 1; while (i >= 0 && !bad[i]) i--; tm = i + 1; }
      return { rows, peak: Math.max(...win.map((r) => r.load)), passed: avg((r) => r.reach / r.total), blocked: avg((r) => r.blocked), tm, minEdge: Math.min(...win.map((r) => r.okEdge)), directLoad: Math.max(...win.map((r) => r.directLoad)), chalAt };
    }
    // SIM-END
    const MANY_BLOCKED = 0.1; const SOME_BLOCKED = 0.03; const TOO_MANY_BLOCKED = 0.25; const MANY_PASSED = 0.1; // verdict thresholds, shares
    const LOW_RATE_LIMIT = 100; // per-IP limits below this hit shared office addresses
    const THOUSAND = 1000;
    const percent = (x: number) => `${Math.round(x * 100).toLocaleString('en-US')}%`;
    const line1 = q<SVGPolylineElement>('[data-line1]'); const line2 = q<SVGPolylineElement>('[data-line2]');
    const NAMES: Record<string, string> = { http: 'The HTTP flood', bust: 'The cache-busting flood', vol: 'The volumetric flood', slow: 'The low-and-slow attack' };
    function draw() {
      const c: Cfg = { attack: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-attack]').value, pops: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-pops]').value), rate: Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-rate]').value), cache: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cache]').value, chal: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-chal]').value, waf: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-waf]').value, lock: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-lock]').checked };
      q('[data-popsval]').textContent = String(c.pops);
      const r = run(c);
      const edgeGbps = Math.round(K.popGbps * c.pops * K.effect);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${percent(r.peak)} of capacity`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = r.peak > 1 ? 'the origin cannot keep up and starts to fail requests' : 'the origin stays within its capacity';
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${percent(r.blocked)} of real requests`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = `average over the ${K.end - K.start} seconds of the attack, from mistakes of the defences and from overload`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${percent(r.passed)} of attack traffic`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = 'reached the origin, after the edge, the WAF, the challenge and the cache';
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = r.tm === null ? 'never' : r.tm === 0 ? 'no overload' : `${r.tm} s`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = r.tm === null ? 'the origin or the edge is still overloaded when the attack ends' : r.tm === 0 ? `the edge handles up to ${edgeGbps} Gbps of attack at once` : 'seconds from the start of the attack until the load stays within capacity';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', r.peak > 1 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', r.blocked > MANY_BLOCKED ? 'var(--bad)' : r.blocked > SOME_BLOCKED ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', r.passed > MANY_PASSED ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', r.tm === null ? 'var(--bad)' : r.tm > 0 ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--good)');
      line1.setAttribute('points', r.rows.map((x) => `${(x.t * 4).toFixed(1)},${(62 - Math.min(3, x.load) * 20.67).toFixed(1)}`).join(' '));
      line2.setAttribute('points', r.rows.map((x) => `${(x.t * 4).toFixed(1)},${(62 - Math.min(1, x.blocked) * 54).toFixed(1)}`).join(' '));
      const out = q('[data-verdict]');
      const name = NAMES[c.attack];
      let msg = ''; let bad = false;
      if (r.tm === null) {
        bad = true;
        if (!c.lock && r.directLoad > 1) msg = `${name} found the origin address and went around the edge, so no rate limit, WAF, challenge or cache ever saw it. Turn on the lockdown so the origin accepts only the edge.`;
        else if (r.minEdge < EDGE_OK) {
          const cap = c.attack === 'vol' ? `${edgeGbps} Gbps` : c.attack === 'slow' ? `${Math.round((K.popConns * c.pops * K.effect) / THOUSAND)}k open connections` : `${Math.round((K.popRps * c.pops * K.effect) / THOUSAND)}k requests per second`;
          msg = `The edge itself ran out of capacity: ${c.pops} ${c.pops === 1 ? 'point' : 'points'} of presence absorb${c.pops === 1 ? 's' : ''} about ${cap} when an attack is concentrated, and the flood is bigger. Real users share the same links and tables, so they fail with the attack. ${c.attack === 'slow' ? 'Add points of presence, or use a WAF setting that times out slow clients sooner.' : 'Add points of presence.'}`;
        }
        else if (c.attack === 'bust' && c.cache === 'full') msg = `Every request has a new random query string, so a cache keyed by the full URL never hits and every request goes to the origin. Normalize the cache key so unknown query parameters are ignored.`;
        else if (c.cache === 'off') msg = `With the cache off, every real request that is not blocked goes to the origin, and so does the ${percent(r.passed)} of ${name.toLowerCase()} that the filters let through. Turn the cache on.`;
        else msg = `${name} still gets ${percent(r.passed)} of its traffic to the origin. Per-IP limits cannot see a botnet where each address sends only ${ATTACKS[c.attack].perIp} requests per second. ${c.chal === 'off' ? 'Score the clients: use a stricter WAF or turn on the challenge.' : 'The challenge and the WAF still let too much through, so tighten the WAF or add origin capacity.'}`;
        if (r.blocked > MANY_BLOCKED) msg += ` Meanwhile ${percent(r.blocked)} of real requests failed.`;
      } else if (r.blocked > TOO_MANY_BLOCKED) {
        bad = true;
        msg = `The origin is safe${r.tm > 0 ? ` after ${r.tm} seconds` : ''}, but the defences blocked ${percent(r.blocked)} of real requests, which is the cost of being wrong. ${c.rate > 0 && c.rate < LOW_RATE_LIMIT ? 'A low per-IP limit hits shoppers behind shared office addresses and busy page loads. ' : ''}${c.waf === 'strict' ? 'A strict WAF rejects some real customers. ' : ''}Look for a setting that stops the attack with fewer mistakes.`;
      } else if (r.tm > 0) {
        msg = `Mitigated after ${r.tm} seconds. ${percent(r.blocked)} of real requests were blocked over the attack, mostly while the origin was overloaded and from the challenge. The delay is detection: the shield needs ${K.detect} seconds of overload to be sure, and ${K.push} more to push the rule to every point of presence. Always-on protection avoids the wait but charges real visitors all the time.`;
      } else {
        msg = `${name} never overloads the origin (peak ${percent(r.peak)}) and only ${percent(r.blocked)} of real requests were blocked.${c.chal === 'always' ? ` The always-on challenge costs ${K.chalLoss * 100}% of visitors, even on a quiet day.` : ''}`;
      }
      out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      out.textContent = msg;
    }
    let queued = false;
    const schedule = () => { if (queued) return; queued = true; requestAnimationFrame(() => { queued = false; draw(); }); };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
